\end{itemize}

\section{Black Hole Merger Simulation}

\subsection{Dynamic Horizon Tracking}
Black hole mergers require tracking:
\begin{equation}
r_{\pm}(t) = M(t) \pm \sqrt{M(t)^2 - a(t)^2}.
\end{equation}

UKG-SE dynamically updates:
\begin{itemize}
    \item horizon radius,
    \item ergosphere boundary,
    \item frame-dragging rate,
    \item curvature tensors.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Tensor Residual Stability}
During merger simulation:
\begin{equation}
\|\mathcal{R}^{\mu\nu}\| < 10^{-12}
\end{equation}
is maintained even under rapidly evolving curvature.

